{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 with 512 MiB of zstd-compressed zram swap, active at boot with priority 100 versus disk swap priority -2. Reboot persistence was verified successfully.","actions_performed":["Installed the RHEL 9 zram-generator package.","Created /etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf for a 512 MiB zram0 device using zstd and swap priority 100.","Activated and verified the generated swap unit.","Safely rebooted node1 once and verified its boot identity changed.","Confirmed zram and disk swap recovered after reboot with no failed systemd units."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"At least 512 MB of compressed in-memory swap","command_ids":["cmd-3c8aea16e39b4e32","cmd-818f570b45834950"],"summary":"/dev/zram0 reports 536,870,912 bytes with zstd selected and is active."},{"requirement":"Preferred over disk-backed swap","command_ids":["cmd-cc071bbc3fbb49d2","cmd-818f570b45834950"],"summary":"zram priority is 100 while /dev/vda2 disk swap priority is -2."},{"requirement":"Active at boot","command_ids":["cmd-cc071bbc3fbb49d2","cmd-818f570b45834950"],"summary":"Pre-reboot generator wiring targets swap.target; after reboot, dev-zram0.swap and its setup service are active."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-cc071bbc3fbb49d2","cmd-88c3c812686f45c1","cmd-72ec0970aa124be1","cmd-818f570b45834950"],"summary":"Healthy baseline used boot ID 0305efed-2c0e-4265-b609-10e8259d59a7; reboot was acknowledged; the new boot ID is c60dfc3f-c94a-47f5-b7b2-321f6c44442a; configuration, both swap devices, zram size/compression/priority, and system health recovered."}]}
